From 8b73a0490381cf181bf60e80adb45aca23c19869 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ferdinand Vanmaele <info@fvanmaele.de>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 03:39:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] [clangd] Answer definitions and references from the index
 shard before parsing

Go-to-definition and find-references wait for the file's AST (runWithAST).
For files with large preambles this is several seconds after opening, even
though the background index already stored, for this file, every reference
with its position, built from a full parse.

With the new hidden flag --navigation-from-index, ClangdServer first loads the
file's background-index shard. If the open file's content has the shard's
digest (and the shard was built without errors), the symbol under the cursor
is found among the shard's references and the request is answered from the
index, without an AST. Positions the shard does not record (keywords such as
auto, function-local symbols, #include lines, macros) and edited files take
the AST path as before. Requests asking for containers keep the AST path.

- BackgroundIndex::loadShard(File) exposes the stored shard.
- XRefs: symbolAtFromShard, locateSymbolFromShard, findReferencesFromShard.
- Tests compare shard answers with the AST answers for the same code.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
